{"subject": {"registry": "entities", "key": "entity-54216265301484356956"}, "aspect": "life-of-states", "statement": "Saving a policy to a local or user-specific policy file raises the Group Policy version stamp by 1 (machine) or 65536 (user), or writes 65537 when absent or the file is new. This changes no setting state. Saving to a plain POL file, a user registry hive or the live registry leaves the stamp alone.", "basis": {"observed": {"evidence": [{"lines": {"file": "PolicyPlus/PolicyLoader.vb", "firstLine": 173, "lastLine": 207}, "shows": "The version line is incremented or created; no setting state is touched."}, {"lines": {"file": "PolicyPlus/PolicyLoader.vb", "firstLine": 117, "lastLine": 147}, "shows": "The stamp is written only on local and security-identifier policy saves."}]}}}
{"subject": {"registry": "entities", "key": "entity-54216265301484356956"}, "aspect": "life-of-states", "statement": "A save to the local policy file where the machine has no Group Policy service applies queued deletions and key clearances straight to the registry, which holds neither state. Such saves with the service present leave the file's states for the service to apply.", "basis": {"observed": {"evidence": [{"lines": {"file": "PolicyPlus/PolicyLoader.vb", "firstLine": 125, "lastLine": 133}, "shows": "Without the infrastructure, the POL difference is applied to the registry at once."}, {"lines": {"file": "PolicyPlus/PolicySource.vb", "firstLine": 150, "lastLine": 175}, "shows": "Deletion and clearance entries become registry deletes."}]}}}
